# Ignore everything at the repo root by default
/*

# ...except these files
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/package.json
!/vercel.json
!/AGENTS.md
!/CONTEXT.md

# Directories the build will live in — un-ignored up front so
# future code pushes without editing this file
!/app/
!/api/
!/pipeline/
!/.github/

# Local cartographic prototype exports — keep available for development, but
# do not include them in the repository until their publication contract lands.
/pipeline/maps/

# Windows/agent safety scripts (worktree/data guards) — versioned
!/scripts/

# The published payload (public/data/ at the repo root) is the product's
# artifact — committed and served by the static host (ADR-0004). The
# pipeline's raw and produced data (pipeline/data/) stays gitignored.
!/public/
# Territory read models are release artifacts alongside the canonical payload.
# Vite may project them in memory during development, but published models must
# remain visible to the pipeline's `git add public/data` release step.

# ADRs — the decisions the code cites — are versioned, like their
# siblings (docs/adr/0001..0003); the rest of docs/ stays local
!/docs/
/api/.env
/api/__pycache__/
/api/**/__pycache__/
/api/.pytest_cache/
/docs/*
!/docs/adr/
# Le prototype #499 (jetable) : son dossier de revue — README + captures —
# est l'artefact de décision versionné, comme les rapports d'audit des
# PRs #451/#452/#455/#491.
!/docs/prototypes/
